{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Go from opposite him</b> — when the word is linked with mem it connotes distance; when with lamed it indicates nearness to something. The mem serves for two, like the mem of \"from your father's El\" — that is, go from opposite him and distance yourself from a man who is a fool and without knowledge, who is a man of lips of knowledge — as if it said distance yourself from him, meaning from a man whom you have not known to be wise."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:42.076379002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}